  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The discovery of the Dead Sea Scrolls in 1947 revolutionized our understanding of the history of Judaism. The scrolls, which date back to around 150 BCE, contain biblical texts, apocryphal works, and other writings that were thought to be lost forever. One of the most significant finds was a copy of the Book of Enoch, a text considered canonical by some Jewish sects but not accepted into the Hebrew Bible.\n\nThe scrolls also include fragments of the Book of Jubilees, which describes the creation of the world in 7 days and the history of humanity until the time of Abraham. Other texts reveal the existence of various Jewish sects that flourished during this period, including the Essenes, who lived in the Qumran community near the Dead Sea.\n\nThe significance of these discoveries lies not only in their age but also in their content. They provide a unique window into the spiritual and intellectual debates of ancient Judaism, shedding light on the development of Jewish thought and practice. Moreover, they demonstrate that the Jewish tradition was far more diverse than previously believed, with different groups holding varying interpretations of scripture.\n\nThe Dead Sea Scrolls have had a profound impact on our understanding of the history of Judaism, forcing scholars to reevaluate their assumptions about the development of Jewish thought and practice. They also underscore the importance of preserving cultural heritage and the value of archaeological discoveries in illuminating the past.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What was a significant find among the Dead Sea Scrolls?\",\n      \"options\": [\"A copy of the Book of Enoch\", \"Fragments of the Book of Jubilees\", \"The Hebrew Bible\", \"A description of the Qumran community\"],\n      \"answer\": \"A copy of the Book of Enoch\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What does the Book of Jubilees describe?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The creation of the world in 6 days\", \"The history of humanity from Adam to Abraham\", \"The life and teachings of Jesus Christ\", \"The history of the Jewish people during the Babylonian exile\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The history of humanity from Adam to Abraham\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What do the Dead Sea Scrolls reveal about ancient Judaism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"That it was a single, unified faith\", \"That it had no diversity or variation in thought and practice\", \"That different groups held varying interpretations of scripture\", \"That it was not influenced by other cultures\"],\n      \"answer\": \"That different groups held varying interpretations of scripture\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What impact have the Dead Sea Scrolls had on our understanding of Jewish history?\",\n      \"options\": [\"They have confirmed many existing theories about Jewish thought and practice\", \"They have forced scholars to reevaluate their assumptions about the development of Jewish thought and practice\", \"They have provided no new insights into Jewish history\", \"They have shown that the Hebrew Bible is a completely accurate account of Jewish history\"],\n      \"answer\": \"They have forced scholars to reevaluate their assumptions about the development of Jewish thought and practice\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What does the author suggest is the value of preserving cultural heritage?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It allows us to forget our past\", \"It has no practical application in modern life\", \"It helps us understand the development of thought and practice\", \"It is a waste of time and resources\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It helps us understand the development of thought and practice\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
